# Seller Auction Actions - Walkthrough

I have implemented the seller auction actions as requested. Here's a summary of the changes:

## New Files Created

| File | Purpose |
|------|---------|
| [AuctionCancelledEvent.java](file:///e:/Web_Application/backend/src/main/java/com/example/backend/event/AuctionCancelledEvent.java) | Event for auction cancellation |
| [EditAuctionRequest.java](file:///e:/Web_Application/backend/src/main/java/com/example/backend/auction/domain/auction/dto/EditAuctionRequest.java) | DTO for edit auction request |
| [ReopenAuctionRequest.java](file:///e:/Web_Application/backend/src/main/java/com/example/backend/auction/domain/auction/dto/ReopenAuctionRequest.java) | DTO for reopen auction request |
| [SchemaFixer.java](file:///e:/Web_Application/backend/src/main/java/com/example/backend/config/SchemaFixer.java) | DB schema updater for new ENUM values |

## Modified Files

### [TransactionType.java](file:///e:/Web_Application/backend/src/main/java/com/example/backend/payment/entity/TransactionType.java)
Added `SALE_INCOME` for tracking seller revenue.

### [AuctionEndService.java](file:///e:/Web_Application/backend/src/main/java/com/example/backend/auction/service/AuctionEndService.java)
- Added payment transfer logic (buyer → seller)
- Added [cancelAuction()](file:///e:/Web_Application/backend/src/main/java/com/example/backend/auction/service/AuctionEndService.java#102-130) method for refunding all bidders
- Both buyer and seller get transaction records

### [RefundWorker.java](file:///e:/Web_Application/backend/src/main/java/com/example/backend/auction/service/RefundWorker.java)
Added handler for [AuctionCancelledEvent](file:///e:/Web_Application/backend/src/main/java/com/example/backend/event/AuctionCancelledEvent.java#6-24) to refund all bidders when auction is cancelled.

### [AuctionWriteService.java](file:///e:/Web_Application/backend/src/main/java/com/example/backend/auction/service/AuctionWriteService.java)
- Added [editAuction()](file:///e:/Web_Application/backend/src/main/java/com/example/backend/auction/controller/AuctionSellerController.java#198-219) - updates title (regenerates slug), prices
- Added [reopenAuction()](file:///e:/Web_Application/backend/src/main/java/com/example/backend/auction/controller/AuctionSellerController.java#281-302) - reopens closed auction with new dates

### [AuctionSellerController.java](file:///e:/Web_Application/backend/src/main/java/com/example/backend/auction/controller/AuctionSellerController.java)
New endpoints:

| Endpoint | Action |
|----------|--------|
| `PUT /api/seller/auctions/{id}` | Edit auction details |
| `POST /api/seller/auctions/{id}/early-end` | End auction early (winner gets deal) |
| `POST /api/seller/auctions/{id}/cancel` | Cancel auction (refund all) |
| `POST /api/seller/auctions/{id}/reopen` | Reopen closed auction |

## Key Design Decisions

> [!IMPORTANT]
> All auction endings go through `AuctionEndService.processAuctionEnd()` to ensure proper Deal creation, refunds, and emails.

1. **Early End**: Calls the same [processAuctionEnd()](file:///e:/Web_Application/backend/src/main/java/com/example/backend/auction/service/AuctionEndService.java#42-101) that the scheduler uses
2. **Cancel**: Uses new [cancelAuction()](file:///e:/Web_Application/backend/src/main/java/com/example/backend/auction/service/AuctionEndService.java#102-130) method that refunds ALL bidders
3. **Payment Transfer**: When auction ends successfully, money is transferred from buyer to seller with transaction records for both
4. **Reopen**: Only works for `Closed` auctions (no winner, no money involved)

## API Usage Examples

### Edit Auction
```http
PUT /api/seller/auctions/123
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "title": "New Title",
  "startingPrice": 100000,
  "minStep": 10000,
  "buyNowPrice": 500000
}
```

### Early End
```http
POST /api/seller/auctions/123/early-end
```

### Cancel Auction
```http
POST /api/seller/auctions/123/cancel
```

### Reopen Auction
```http
POST /api/seller/auctions/123/reopen
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "startDate": "2025-12-07T10:00:00",
  "endDate": "2025-12-14T18:00:00"
}
```
